---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "About me";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section class="py-12">
    <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-[68ch]">
      <p>
        I'm a junior software engineer based in Bristol, working across
        embedded systems and cloud/backend development. My degree in Computer
        Science at Lancaster University leaned heavily into distributed and
        embedded systems &mdash; C, Assembly, GPIO, I2C, UART, EEPROM &mdash;
        and that low-level curiosity still shapes most of what I build. I also
        completed the Code Institute Full Stack Developer Bootcamp, which gave
        me a Django-focused grounding in web development.
      </p>

      <h2>Technical journey</h2>
      <p>
        Rust is the common thread through my current work. I rebuilt the
        backend of my AWS Cloud Resume Challenge as a Rust Lambda, cutting
        cold starts by over 97% and response times from roughly 140ms down to
        6&ndash;8ms, and later migrated the frontend to Cloudflare Pages after
        an AWS billing scare taught me not to keep all my eggs in one
        provider's basket. On the systems side, I'm building a Game Boy
        emulator in Rust from scratch &mdash; CPU emulation, cycle-accurate
        timers, memory mapping, and now working towards getting Tetris
        running. I've also worked with Django and Spring/React, including
        leading the technical build of a booking platform during a
        three-day hackathon.
      </p>

      <h2>Professional development</h2>
      <p>
        I stay involved in the tech community by attending industry talks.
        They keep my curiosity fed, introduce me to new people, and help me
        keep up with where software development is heading.
      </p>

      <h2>Community impact</h2>
      <p>
        I've volunteered helping elderly community members bridge the digital
        divide &mdash; maintaining their computers and teaching them to use
        essential online services.
      </p>

      <h2>Life outside tech</h2>
      <p>
        Away from the keyboard, I'm usually baking &mdash; cakes, gooey
        chocolate brownies, you name it &mdash; walking the paths at
        Westonbirt Arboretum, or working through French (currently somewhere
        around A1-A2). Stepping away from a problem is often what makes the
        solution obvious when I come back to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Current focus</h2>
      <p>
        Right now I'm deepening my embedded and systems programming skills
        while finishing the Game Boy emulator, and applying for junior
        embedded and cloud/backend roles. I've also been building and
        deploying Focus Companion, an ADHD-friendly focus app with a Next.js
        frontend on Vercel and a Spring backend on Heroku, using Clerk for
        auth, Postgres for storage, and Docker throughout &mdash; with data
        now encrypted at rest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>